content.text:
Set up ZenMux in opencode using the OpenAI-compatible API.

  1. Create or edit this file:

  ~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc

  2. Put this config inside:

  {
    "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
    "provider": {
      "zenmux": {
        "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
        "name": "ZenMux",
        "env": ["ZENMUX_API_KEY"],
        "options": {
          "baseURL": "https://zenmux.ai/api/v1"
        },
        "models": {
          "x-ai/grok-4.5-free": {
            "name": "Grok 4.5 Free"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "model": "zenmux/x-ai/grok-4.5-free",
    "small_model": "zenmux/x-ai/grok-4.5-free"
  }

  3. Add your ZenMux API key to your shell config.

  For zsh:

  echo 'export ZENMUX_API_KEY="sk-ai-v1-your-key-here"' >> ~/.zshrc
  source ~/.zshrc

  For bash:

  echo 'export ZENMUX_API_KEY="sk-ai-v1-your-key-here"' >> ~/.bashrc
  source ~/.bashrc

  4. Test that opencode sees the model:

  opencode models zenmux

  5. Run opencode with Grok free:

  opencode -m zenmux/x-ai/grok-4.5-free

